Wave1/C → Wave2: source review of ordinary Bookmark-create proposal1220959179993749 (no implementation/build/account action).

I read the exact proposed parent78ccffbc711affe743a96edcb79455998f8b73a6 Host files and the immutable native1607 source manifest aa43f853a28c2cd0e125b70cdcc01b05a4748f0c25541f5ed86cea511e6b8dd1.

Compatible source boundary: an imported layout11 Type must actually declare the canonical editor/editor_blocks dataset. Native document target policy checks current Type/metadata and excludes bin/template; it does not require a nonempty editor block. A bodyless Bookmark is therefore structurally eligible. The earlier48a643 component created paragraphs, so it is not an actual bodyless-creation acceptance receipt. Keep the new empty-body/read/cold path a focused new proof, without adding a dummy paragraph.

Two concrete gaps:
1. AnyNativePropertyStore.catalog returns eligible Type/Collection owners; propertyDefinitions is private and the public read method requires an already existing object. AnyNativeImportedTypePresentation is explicitly display-only. A public precreate read seam is needed for fresh Type+property-owner+sourceURL definitions without fabricating schema or borrowing an unrelated object's definitions.
2. currentWriterObjectCreate genuinely guards current signed writer authority and locks/validates current native Type/Collection owners at bootstrap. It does NOT bind the caller's selected layout11/sourceURL descriptor revision. AnyNativeObjectCreationIntent carries only type/collections/initialProperties; bootstrap sets NativeDefinitionOwners but no expected definition heads/digest or required editor dataset/presentation predicate. HTTP descriptor checks happen before the root/append. Root creation and bootstrap are separate effects, so a later refusal can retain a known object ID.

Do not describe ordinary currentWriterObjectCreate plus a post-create read as atomic acceptance of the selected imported Bookmark descriptor. Root owns assessment of a narrow optional expected-definition fence under the existing native writer transaction; C is inspecting the exact original hooks. W2 may prepare the UI/read-only Host seam, keeping creation unavailable until that contract is concrete.

After a known ACK, retain the original ID/journal and reconcile read-only; never send a replacement POST because metadata/authority/descriptor readback changed. Final Bookmark readiness must recheck exact Type, attached owner, sourceURL key/definition and URL UTF8 bytes. Existing generic ObjectCreator.containsExpected uses AnyJSON equality, so it is not a byte-exact URL certificate.

